DESCRIPTION Peer-errors band, oversized tool result: the answer sits at the tail of a 1500-row inventory that a reader may truncate and then summarize from partial data.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "The host inventory is the ConfigMap peer-errors-fixture-host-inventory in the crew-homelab-pilot namespace (key inventory.csv, one row per host). How many hosts are marked decommissioned, and which ones?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 720 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic: the three decommissioned rows are all in the last 10 percent of the file (rows 1337, 1412, 1493 of 1500).
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "1337" AND "1412" AND "1493")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "no decommissioned")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "none are decommissioned")

ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The inventory (a test fixture) has 1500 rows, host-0001 to host-1500. Exactly three are decommissioned: host-1337, host-1412 and host-1493, all near the end of the file. A tool result of this size is likely to be cut off before the end. A correct, verified answer finds all three (by filtering or searching the rows, not by reading the head of the file), reports the count 3 and the three names, and if it could read only part of the data says so instead of reporting a count from the part it saw. Reporting none, reporting fewer than three, or naming hosts that are not decommissioned misses; so does an answer that presents a partial read as complete. Scored: the answer covers the whole inventory or says it did not.")
